{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "orca",
  "name": "Orca",
  "note": "A desktop workspace that runs agents in its own managed terminals. Sessions come from `orca terminal list --json`, which reports the live terminals with the agent each one is running; the Electron app's own storage is a browser profile and not a session record. Focus goes through `orca terminal switch`, because raising the application would show whichever tab it had open rather than the session that was clicked. The agent actually running in a terminal is `agentIdentity`, so a Codex pane and a Claude pane are told apart rather than both reported as Orca.",
